<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmadil ibn Ibrahim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1116</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmadil ibn Ibrahim was a Kurdish emir of the Rawwadid family who held Maragheh in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> under the Seljuk sultans. He was one of the leading Seljuk commanders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and joined the campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1111. He was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1116 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a>, and his former mamluk Aq Sunqur founded a dynasty named after him.</p></div>
